     Default: 0.2 (200 ms).
 
+``--audio-crossfade-duration=<seconds>``
+    Automatically cross-fade between queued audio playlist entries. Accepts
+    0 to 30 seconds; zero disables automatic transitions (the default). Set
+    this before loading a file. It reserves decoded PCM lookahead itself;
+    ``--audio-crossfade-buffer`` is not required for automatic mode.
+
+    The core prepares the next entry with the existing playlist prefetcher,
+    waits until the final PCM window is decoded, and opens the next decoder
+    while retained outgoing audio plays. The output mixer applies the overlap
+    per sample. The playlist is preserved, and its loop and shuffle policy is
+    applied once per transition. An outgoing transition reports natural EOF.
+
+    This is for forward audio playback, including cover art. Video, encoding,
+    unsupported outputs, active A-B loops, explicit playback end ranges,
+    remaining file loops, frame stepping and ``--keep-open=always`` retain
+    ordinary end-of-file behavior. Pausing or a pending transport fade defers
+    the transition. Seeking or stopping cancels a retained overlap.
+
+    The overlap is limited by decoded PCM, incoming decoder readiness, and
+    the 64 MiB outgoing reserve. A short incoming file shortens the overlap
+    without trimming the outgoing file's end. Online playback remains
+    best-effort. Lookahead increases memory and buffering; changes to this
+    option during playback reconfigure the audio output.
+
+``--audio-crossfade-curve=<linear|equal-power>``
+    Curve for automatic playlist overlaps (default: linear). Equal-power uses
+    sine/cosine gains and may require extra peak headroom. This does not change
+    ordinary transport fades or the curve argument of ``crossfade-loadfile``.
+
 ``--audio-crossfade-buffer=<seconds>``
     Reserve additional decoded PCM lookahead for ``crossfade-loadfile``. Accepts
     0 to 30 seconds, limited to 64 MiB according to the output format. Zero is
